  "dom_id": "step-q82372",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the exact solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(x-{90}^{\u2218})=-1$ for ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218},$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$",
  "worked_solution": "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-{90}^{\u2218} & =-{45}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={90}^{\u2218}-{45}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218} \\\\ x & ={45}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\u2026,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={45}^{\u2218}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={225}^{\u2218}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218}.$ So, the solutions are $x={45}^{\u2218},{225}^{\u2218}.$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is $45\\cdot 225=10\\,125.$",
